    <!-- Does this load get the boot skeleton? Decided HERE, in the head,
         before the element it governs has even been parsed.

         ⚠ IT USED TO SIT AT THE END OF THE BODY AND REMOVE `hidden`, WHICH IS A
         RACE. A browser may paint a first frame mid-parse, and any frame taken
         between the skeleton's markup and a reveal that comes after it is the
         black background — the exact flash this was built to remove, now
         arriving from the mechanism meant to prevent it. Deciding in the head
         means no frame can exist with the answer unknown. Same reason a
         dark-mode class is set in the head rather than after the page.

         Fail-safe in the same direction as before: the CSS default is hidden
         and this switches it ON, so a blocked or broken script leaves the old
         black screen rather than stamping a dashboard over a login page.

         The paths are `sectionPath()`'s own (src/lib/app-routes.ts): recent is
         the bare root, My boards is /boards, and a team prefixes /t/<slug>.
         Library, settings, boards and the rest are deliberately NOT here — they
         draw a different shell, and the React skeleton covers them a moment
         later.

         The use-case doors (/use/<slug>, a page a paid ad lands on, usually on a
         phone) get no skeleton but a LIGHT GROUND from the first frame
         (`data-boot-ground`): their page is light, and the black base showed for
         the seconds the bundle took on a phone (Dor, 2026-10-01: "make sure we
         never have black borders").

         CSP: allowed by a sha256 hash in apps/web/vercel.json (script-src),
         exactly like the boot watchdog above. ANY byte change below breaks the
         hash and the skeleton silently stops appearing early. Recompute: sha256
         of the exact text between the script tags, base64. -->
    <script>
      (function () {
        var p = location.pathname.replace(/\/+$/, '') || '/';
        var t = p.indexOf('/t/') === 0 ? p.slice(3).replace(/^[^/]*/, '') || '/' : p;
        if (t === '/' || t === '/dashboard' || t === '/boards' || t === '/recent' || t === '/shared') {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-boot-skeleton', 'on');
        }
        if (p.indexOf('/use/') === 0) {
          document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-boot-ground', 'light');
        }
      })();
    </script>
